{
  "id": "math_capability_shapes",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "description": "SHAPE-COMPARABLE SIGNATURES (graph data) for the math<->capability BRIDGE. Each node names a held MATH Concept OR a held FACULTY and carries its STRUCTURAL SIGNATURE as a relation-system (positional tuples, the form the held order-N shape-matcher AntiUnify consumes). The bridge faculty runs the HELD AntiUnify over two named signatures and reads out the shared structural skeleton (the connection) + discriminates by FixedCount. The signature is the item's OWN mathematical structure written in the agent's relation vocabulary (build/refers/bound/base/detect/...), NOT a hardcoded 'fractal=residual' string; the connection is whatever AntiUnify finds the two SHARE. Extensible: add a ShapeSignature node to make a new math or faculty bridgeable.",
